From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: add battery

Add the CW2217 fuel gauge found at 0x64 on the charger I2C bus, so the
device reports a battery to userspace.

The design values come from the vendor tree: fcc_design = 5000 (mAh) in
the CW2217 battery profile, and the 3400 mV / 4450 mV low and high voltage
alarm points that downstream programs into the gauge.

The two other chips on this bus, an SGM41542 charger at 0x3b and an
SGM7220 Type-C controller at 0x47, are left out for now: neither has a
driver, and the charger in particular must not be poked blindly.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -142,6 +142,18 @@
 		pinctrl-0 = <&panel_vci_default>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Design values from the vendor tree: fcc_design in the CW2217
+	 * battery profile, and the low/high voltage alarm points that
+	 * downstream programs into the gauge.
+	 */
+	battery: battery {
+		compatible = "simple-battery";
+		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5000000>;
+		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
+		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4450000>;
+	};
+
 	touch_avdd: touch-avdd-regulator {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "touch_avdd";
@@ -177,6 +189,18 @@
 &i2c8 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * Also on this bus, not yet supported: an SGM41542 charger at 0x3b
+	 * and an SGM7220 Type-C controller at 0x47.
+	 */
+	fuel-gauge@64 {
+		compatible = "cellwise,cw2217";
+		reg = <0x64>;
+		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+		shunt-resistor-micro-ohms = <5000>;
+		cellwise,ui-full-soc = <97>;
+	};
 };
 
 &i2c10 {
